{"name":"Black Oak","hex":"#4e4f4e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black oak","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deciduous oak tree, Quercus velutina, native to eastern North America; its wood.","A related oak tree native to western North America, Quercus kelloggii, often considered the best oak for acorn mush by American Indians in its native range; the wood of this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_oak"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black Oak, Arkansas","blocks":[{"text":"Black Oak is a town in Craighead County, Arkansas, United States. The population was 233 in the 2020 census. It is included in the Jonesboro, Arkansas Metropolitan Statistical Area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Black_Oak_AR_005.jpg/330px-Black_Oak_AR_005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Oak%2C_Arkansas","wikidata":"Q2901359"},{"title":"Black Oak, Daviess County, Indiana","blocks":[{"text":"Black Oak is a small unincorporated community in Barr Township, Daviess County, Indiana."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Oak%2C_Daviess_County%2C_Indiana","wikidata":"Q4921394"},{"title":"Black Oak (Gary, Indiana)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Oak is a neighborhood located on the far southwest side of Gary, Indiana. As of 2000, Black Oak had a population of 4,216, which was 84.7% white. It is Gary's only majority-white neighborhood, and the most recent neighborhood added to the city. Black Oak was annexed in 1976, under the administration of mayor Richard Hatcher. Prior to that, Black Oak had been an unincorporated area informally associated with nearby Hammond, and the area has Hammond telephone numbers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/US-IN-Gary-Black-Oak.png/330px-US-IN-Gary-Black-Oak.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Oak_(Gary%2C_Indiana)","wikidata":"Q4921395"},{"title":"Black oak","blocks":[{"text":"Black oak is a common name for several species of tree. These include:"},{"items":["Quercus kelloggii, the California black oak, from the western United States","Quercus velutina, the eastern black oak, from the eastern United States and Canada","Casuarina pauper, an Australian tree species","Trigonobalanus excelsa, the Colombian black oak, an oak relative from Colombia"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_oak","wikidata":"Q25114100"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Black_Oak_AR_007.jpg/250px-Black_Oak_AR_007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Black_Oak_AR_007.jpg/330px-Black_Oak_AR_007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Black_Oak_AR_007.jpg/250px-Black_Oak_AR_007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Oak_AR_007.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Black_Oak_AR_008.jpg/250px-Black_Oak_AR_008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Black_Oak_AR_008.jpg/330px-Black_Oak_AR_008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Black_Oak_AR_008.jpg/250px-Black_Oak_AR_008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Oak_AR_008.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating 2","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/The_Indian_grey_mongoose